{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or","id":1514646,"title":"Additional books, or.....?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-11T20:33:31-07:00","id":1514646,"title":"Additional books, or.....?","content":"So I was looking at the list of products and noticed that nothing has come out in the past couple years and I was just wondering if there are any plans for additional material, or if it's all put on hold for the chance of Renegade doing a Changeling 5th?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T21:54:09-07:00","id":1514649,"title":"","content":"Changeling only had 3 core editions so shouldn't be Changeling 4th?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:43:36-07:00","id":1514666,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Reckoning only had one original edition as we're still calling the new things H5.<br /> <br /> We're unlikely to see much new material:<br /> <br /> 1) Dreaming was a fairly small game and C20 covered a lot of ground with a small number of supplements.<br /> 2) Paradox has been pretty harsh towards new 20th books unless they're things that tie into the WoD5 era stuff (so we might see a C20 equivalent to Beckett's Jyhad Diary and Apocalyptic Record when C5 is closer to coming out).<br /> 3) Because of 2, a lot of CtD freelancers just make stuff on the Storyteller's Vault; so it's not official material, but it's probably what we'd get if Paradox would be more supportive of the 20th book lines that aren't getting a WoD5 era book in the near future.<br /> 4) The lead developer of C20 was blackballed from Onyx Path and any place seeking some sense of moral decency for being a sexual predator; including abuse targeted at at least one of the C20 writers. That didn't really leave the team that worked on C20 intact to keep up the pitches like W20 did (unlil Stew Wilson quit) or M20 has managed with Brucato pushing a lot of book pitches through fast before Paradox started to wind things down.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to be a downer on that last point, but it's hard to contextualize why C20 didn't try for more without addressing that part of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:43:11-07:00","id":1514750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1514666#post1514666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter: the Reckoning only had one original edition as we're still calling the new things H5.<br /> <br /> We're unlikely to see much new material:<br /> <br /> 1) Dreaming was a fairly small game and C20 covered a lot of ground with a small number of supplements.<br /> 2) Paradox has been pretty harsh towards new 20th books unless they're things that tie into the WoD5 era stuff (so we might see a C20 equivalent to Beckett's Jyhad Diary and Apocalyptic Record when C5 is closer to coming out).<br /> 3) Because of 2, a lot of CtD freelancers just make stuff on the Storyteller's Vault; so it's not official material, but it's probably what we'd get if Paradox would be more supportive of the 20th book lines that aren't getting a WoD5 era book in the near future.<br /> 4) The lead developer of C20 was blackballed from Onyx Path and any place seeking some sense of moral decency for being a sexual predator; including abuse targeted at at least one of the C20 writers. That didn't really leave the team that worked on C20 intact to keep up the pitches like W20 did (unlil Stew Wilson quit) or M20 has managed with Brucato pushing a lot of book pitches through fast before Paradox started to wind things down.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to be a downer on that last point, but it's hard to contextualize why C20 didn't try for more without addressing that part of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I totally get it. I had totally forgotten who the lead developer was for C20. Thats trash. (Not the blackballing. That was totally justified.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T02:54:40-07:00","id":1514931,"title":"","content":"That said, and further to Heavy Arms point 3, the C20 books on Storytellers Vault are almost all written by the freelancers who worked on C20 and have stated that they are the books they would have proposed if Paradox hadn't killed the line prematurely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T13:49:58-07:00","id":1515011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1514931#post1514931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, and further to Heavy Arms point 3, the C20 books on Storytellers Vault are almost all written by the freelancers who worked on C20 and have stated that they are the books they would have proposed if Paradox hadn't killed the line prematurely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know. I'll definitely check them out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T15:17:43-07:00","id":1515024,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I think it would be useful to set up and maintain a sticky topic in this forum linking to all of the C20 STV products written by the C20 team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T11:49:05-07:00","id":1515547,"title":"","content":"If there's a list of who those people are I don't mind digging through the site to get links to their supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T14:12:48-07:00","id":1515564,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Charlie%20Cantrell\" target=\"_blank\">Charlie Cantrell</a> wrote for both C20 core and C20 Player's Guide; he's also involved in C20 Book of Freeholds, Harbingers of Winter, Kiths of Arcadia, Fragments of the Lycian Dream, and Past is Prologue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T13:39:31-07:00","id":1518200,"title":"","content":"It would be ideal to switch to C5 created by Charlie Cantrell, since there are no more C20 announcements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28101-siegvonshroeder","name":"SiegVonShroeder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T02:15:42-07:00","id":1518224,"title":"","content":"Charile Cantrell's C5 requires C20 to really use anyway, and it could get completely rendered moot if/when the official C5 gets made. Considering there isn't really a bunch of fan-C5 supplements coming out either, there's no real reason to use it unless you really want to use the WoD5 rules instead of the C20 rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T16:03:21-07:00","id":1518458,"title":"","content":"I understand you; however, with the cancellation of the C20 line and the advancements of the fifth edition of Hunter, Vampire, and now Werewolf, it would be great if there were an official C5 line. Or perhaps did the Kithains die with the Long Winter? I ask this because &quot;Time of Judgment&quot; was removed from canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28101-siegvonshroeder","name":"SiegVonShroeder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T17:22:11-07:00","id":1518464,"title":"","content":"Now I wonder, what would they change in a supposed C5? I can't think of a plot that would involve the Changelings with some armed or government-affiliated group, unless they create faerie hunters or the Autumn Folk have decided to become an organization, or maybe the Changelings see a species as being more intimate with people or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T09:02:17-07:00","id":1518642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518224#post1518224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charile Cantrell's C5 requires C20 to really use anyway, and it could get completely rendered moot if/when the official C5 gets made. Considering there isn't really a bunch of fan-C5 supplements coming out either, there's no real reason to use it unless you really want to use the WoD5 rules instead of the C20 rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, hell theres a dozen more C20 books that have come out since the C5 fan splat was released and many of them are high sellers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T16:41:31-07:00","id":1518666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518464#post1518464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I wonder, what would they change in a supposed C5? I can't think of a plot that would involve the Changelings with some armed or government-affiliated group, unless they create faerie hunters or the Autumn Folk have decided to become an organization, or maybe the Changelings see a species as being more intimate with people or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling C5 would end up more like H5 and W5 with more of a reboot than V5's stronger attempt at a direct continuation.<br /> <br /> Something CtD definitely could use is a lesson from CtL (and the CofD in general) less individual groups with more options. I don't think CfD is nearly as wedded to its cultural roots as WtA was, so I think it would be better received to see it cut back on the number of Kiths, types of changelings, and regional rules variations. Let Seeming and Court do more heavy lifting to create the vast variety of character players want without having to sort through massive lists of exclusive options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518642#post1518642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct, hell theres a dozen more C20 books that have come out since the C5 fan splat was released and many of them are high sellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a big point in sticking to C20's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T19:09:54-07:00","id":1518674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518666#post1518666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a feeling C5 would end up more like H5 and W5 with more of a reboot than V5's stronger attempt at a direct continuation.<br /> <br /> Something CtD definitely could use is a lesson from CtL (and the CofD in general) less individual groups with more options. I don't think CfD is nearly as wedded to its cultural roots as WtA was, so I think it would be better received to see it cut back on the number of Kiths, types of changelings, and regional rules variations. Let Seeming and Court do more heavy lifting to create the vast variety of character players want without having to sort through massive lists of exclusive options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, judging from what I know about fifth editions, I think they want to simplify more and CtL kind of does the opposite in that sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T20:07:47-07:00","id":1518675,"title":"","content":"The point I'm making is more that one of the things the CofD does (and WoD5 definitely tries to copy it) is that it's better to have 5 choices from Group A, and 5 choices from Group B, than have a list of 25 options... even though in the end it's actually the same number of options.<br /> <br /> In CtD, there are 21 Kiths just between the Kithain and Gallain. Then you have eight groups of regional Kiths (many of which have unique rules besides just being unique to a given area), six types of Inanimae, and four types of Lycians. And the Thallain. CtL's Kiths are also large, but they're like Predator Types in V5: they're an overlay on top of the base character to create some variation.<br /> <br /> The way to simplify this (and it's something Cantrell's C5 does already) is to reduce that number to more archetypal entries, and create space for variations. Which is what CtL does too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T06:54:19-07:00","id":1518698,"title":"","content":"After the several mentions of it here, I've gone ahead and reviewed Cantrell's C5. While I think some of the changes are unnecessary (in particular, the juggling around of Seeming and Legacy), I could definitely get behind something like that as an official C5. That said, I'm not a fan of the X5 line or mechanics; so I'd be more inclined to extract a few of the gems from it and \u201cbackport\u201d them into C20. Most notable would be the way that thematically related Kiths are collected into seven broad archetypes, as Heavy Arms pointed out; though I'd prefer that they <i>not</i> be called Legacies, as C20 (and older editions) uses that name for something else. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like the \u201cEver Night\u201d metaplot that Cantrell introduces; it's a development that was nicely set up in his \u201cPast is Prologue\u201d STV supplement for Dark Ages: Fae and his \u201cHarbingers of Winter\u201d STV supplement for C20, and which brings a more desperate feel to the setting than the melancholic tone that earlier editions had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T10:56:37-07:00","id":1518713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518698#post1518698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After the several mentions of it here, I've gone ahead and reviewed Cantrell's C5. While I think some of the changes are unnecessary (in particular, the juggling around of Seeming and Legacy), I could definitely get behind something like that as an official C5. That said, I'm not a fan of the X5 line or mechanics; so I'd be more inclined to extract a few of the gems from it and \u201cbackport\u201d them into C20. Most notable would be the way that thematically related Kiths are collected into seven broad archetypes, as Heavy Arms pointed out; though I'd prefer that they <i>not</i> be called Legacies, as C20 (and older editions) uses that name for something else.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like the \u201cEver Night\u201d metaplot that Cantrell introduces; it's a development that was nicely set up in his \u201cPast is Prologue\u201d STV supplement for Dark Ages: Fae and his \u201cHarbingers of Winter\u201d STV supplement for C20, and which brings a more desperate feel to the setting than the melancholic tone that earlier editions had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m inclined to do the same re C20 and replace the Legacies with CTL Seemings.<br /> <br /> Evernight is very cool as is the inclusion of Oaths from DAF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T12:35:02-07:00","id":1518716,"title":"","content":"To be clear: C20's Legacies are equivalent to other gamelines' Nature and Demeanor. That's one reason I object to Cantrell's C20 repurposing the name for \u201cgroupings of similar Kiths\u201d. <br /> <br /> And you might want to consider using Cantrell's Legacies (albeit with some other name for them) instead of CtL's Seekings: the former are Lore Keepers (Eshu, Fu Hsi, Kahuna, Korred, Moir\u00e6, etc.), Makers (Boggans, Hana, Nockers, Wichtel, Yunwi Tsunsdo, etc.), Nobles (Ali'i, Fir-bholg, Merfolk, Oba, Sidhe, etc.), Passionates (Aonides, Morganed, Nyan, Satyrs, Selkies, etc.), Stalwarts (Fuath, Kokua, Rock Giants, Tanuki, Trolls, etc.), Terrors (Naraka, N\u00fcm\u00fczo'ho, Redcaps, River Hags, Sluagh, etc.), and Tricksters (Clurichauns, Hanumen, Piskies, Pooka, Wolpertinger, etc.). The Kiths still gets information defined for Revelry and Unleashing, plus one or two Birthrights and a Frailty; the Legacies themselves \u201cmerely\u201d define a Quest and a Ban, with the former being kind of like a C20 Legacy in that it's a kind of action the changeling can pursue to recover Willpower, and the latter explicitly referencing the Antithesis section in C20 p.269: an action or circumstance that will generate Banality. <br /> <br /> That said, CtL's Seemings and Kiths aren't that bad of a choice, either; although it would take a bit more work to translate them over. Frankly, I really wish we had gotten a Changeling Translation Guide back when there was a window of opportunity to make one: there's <i>lots</i> of stuff from CtL that I'd like to graft onto CtD, and vice versa. And while there's an old fan supplement floating around on the web called Dreams of Delirium (by Angelus Michaels) that incorporates elements from CtD into CtL, I'm unaware of any product that works the other way around. And that's a shame; because as different as the two games are, they <i>do</i> \u201crhyme\u201d. I would <i>love</i> a STV product for CtD that implicitly acts as a \u201cTranslation Guide\u201d from CtL, taking cues from the aforementioned Dreams of Dilirium in how to go about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T14:42:53-07:00","id":1518721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1514646-additional-books-or?p=1518716#post1518716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, CtL's Seemings and Kiths aren't that bad of a choice, either; although it would take a bit more work to translate them over. Frankly, I really wish we had gotten a Changeling Translation Guide back when there was a window of opportunity to make one: there's <i>lots</i> of stuff from CtL that I'd like to graft onto CtD, and vice versa. And while there's an old fan supplement floating around on the web called Dreams of Delirium (by Angelus Michaels) that incorporates elements from CtD into CtL, I'm unaware of any product that works the other way around. And that's a shame; because as different as the two games are, they <i>do</i> \u201crhyme\u201d. I would <i>love</i> a STV product for CtD that implicitly acts as a \u201cTranslation Guide\u201d from CtL, taking cues from the aforementioned Dreams of Dilirium in how to go about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree there\u2019s lots of potential to be taken from CtL into CtD, I\u2019ve got Dreams of Delirium, there\u2019s a load of good stuff that can be ported.<br /> <br /> But agreed a translation guide would be really useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}